I’d like to talk about a time when I had to change a plan unexpectedly.

A few months ago, I was overwhelmed with work and studies, so my friends and I decided to take a short trip to Vũng Tàu to relax. We were all really excited about it because we had been planning it for quite a while. Before the trip, we prepared several things carefully. We searched online for interesting places to visit, local specialties to try, and checked the weather forecast. We even booked our accommodation in advance, so everything seemed perfectly organized.

However, just a few days before the trip, my cousin texted me and said that he was coming to visit me. At first, I felt a bit disappointed because I had been looking forward to the getaway for so long. But then I realized that I hadn’t seen my cousin for years, so I decided to change my plan.

Instead of going to Vũng Tàu, I spent time showing him around Ho Chi Minh City. I took him to some famous attractions and treated him to local dishes so he could experience the lifestyle and culture of the city. We also took lots of photos together to keep as memories.

Surprisingly, the experience turned out to be much more meaningful than I expected. Seeing the smile on my cousin’s face made me really happy, and we had a chance to reconnect and share many memories together.

This experience taught me that life doesn’t always go according to plan, and sometimes being flexible can lead to even better experiences.
